+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` (exported from `src/index.ts`) applies a JSON Merge Patch and returns the
+merged document as a new value.
+
+```ts
+applyMergePatch({ a: "b", c: { d: "e" } }, { a: "z", c: { d: null } }); // { a: "z", c: {} }
+```
+
+- An object patch merges member by member: `null` removes the member, other values merge recursively.
+- A patch that is not an object (including an array or `null`) replaces the target; arrays are replaced whole.
+- A non-object target is treated as `{}` when the patch is an object.
+- Neither argument is mutated and the result shares no structure with either; `__proto__` is a plain member name.
